# ~/.stow-global-ignore — honored by EVERY `stow` run (installer OR manual),
# for every package. Symlinked here by the `stow` package.
#
# IMPORTANT: a global (or package-local) ignore list *replaces* Stow's built-in
# defaults — it does not merge with them. So the defaults we still want are
# re-listed below, followed by our own additions. Perl regexes, one per line;
# a leading '/' anchors to the package root (see the Stow manual, "Types And
# Syntax Of Ignore Lists").

# --- Stow's built-in defaults (kept, since a custom list overrides them) ---
RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules

.+~
\#.*\#

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

# --- Our additions: runtime junk that lives inside packages ---
\.DS_Store
node_modules
package(-lock)?\.json
bun\.lock

\.bak
\.stow-local-ignore
skills-manifest\.json